 "narrative": "This synthesis updates the evidence after delivery of independent validation for the WRN/MSI-high family and the response deadline for SMARCA2/SMARCA4 loss. All reported estimates are used exactly as signed to the claim direction: for direction -1, a positive value means the exposed group has stronger, more negative dependency than the comparator; for direction +1, a positive value means the exposed group has a higher/weaker dependency score.\n\nH16, the main MSI-high versus MSS comparison for WRN dependency, is now independently validated. The discovery estimate was +0.790 (95% CI 0.760 to 0.819), and the independent validation estimate is +0.807 with a very stringent independent interval from +0.759 to +0.855. The lower bound is far from zero and the effect is extremely large relative to the observed WRN dependency-score distribution. This firmly supports, within this supplied dataset, the dataset-level association that MSI-high status is associated with much stronger WRN dependency. It is not evidence of causality or external generalizability, but it is among the strongest findings in the study.\n\nH21, the adenocarcinoma-restricted MSI-high WRN comparison, is also independently validated. The validation estimate is +0.813 (independent CI +0.754 to +0.872), closely matching the discovery subgroup estimate of +0.784. This supports the interpretation that the WRN/MSI-high association is not confined to the non-adenocarcinoma remainder of the dataset and is robust within the dominant adenocarcinoma subset. I keep H21 accepted and close further context investigation because it has achieved independent confirmation and its role as a consistency check for H16 is fulfilled. H16 remains active as a central accepted claim.\n\nH12, SMARCA4 loss versus SMARCA4-intact SMARCA2 dependency, also has independent validation: discovery +0.784 (95% CI 0.765 to 0.803), validation +0.800 (independent CI 0.768 to 0.832). The validation interval excludes zero with large margin and confirms the direction and magnitude. I keep H12 accepted and close its investigation as a validated core association.\n\nAt this point, three of the four strongest main associations are independently validated: SMARCA4 loss with stronger SMARCA2 dependency (H12), KEAP1 loss with weaker NFE2L2 dependency (H17, already validated earlier), and MSI-high status with stronger WRN dependency (H16). The remaining large accepted main association is H15: TP53 wild-type status versus TP53 loss for USP7 dependency. H15 has very strong internal support: overall discovery estimate +0.802 (95% CI 0.782 to 0.822), CDKN2A-intact context +0.800 (R21), and CDKN2A-loss context +0.808 (R31). Nevertheless, it has not yet been independently validated. Given that it is accepted, extremely large, mechanistically coherent, and internally stable across CDKN2A contexts, independent validation of H15 is the highest-priority next evidence request when a validation opportunity arises.\n\nThe negative interaction and specificity work continues to support the specificity of the accepted effects. The WRN effect is not meaningfully modified by adenocarcinoma subtype (H38 rejected), and WRN dependency is not associated with BRCA2 loss (H39 rejected). SMARCA2 and USP7 effects were not meaningfully modified by tested co-alteration or pathway contexts (H23, H26, H29, H37, H40 rejected). NFE2L2/KEAP1 reversal was not modified by TP53 loss or lineage subtype (H42, H43 rejected). Constructed-marker controls for SMARCA2, WRN, USP7, and NFE2L2 were near null (H45-H48), which lowers concern that these large effects are generic artifacts of the constructed assay panels, although specificity against every possible dataset confounder cannot be proven.\n\nNegative findings remain important. Simple binary driver/amplification associations for BRAF V600E, KRAS mutation, ERBB2 amplification, PIK3CA mutation, and TMED10/ERBB2 were rejected. ARID1A main effect on SMARCA2 and MDM2 TP53-pathway associations, including CDKN2A-loss interaction, were rejected. EGFR amplification overall remains unresolved/deferred: the overall estimate was borderline and tested adenocarcinoma and KRAS-wild-type refinements were unconvincing, but H22 remains registered as a possible lineage-interaction test if EGFR is pursued further.\n\nThe most informative next scientific step is to obtain independent validation for H15 while simultaneously registering targeted robustness tests for H15 and H17. I have registered a USP7 TP53-wild-type comparison within KEAP1-loss cells to test whether the USP7 association persists when NRF2 pathway context changes, and a USP7 interaction by lineage subtype to test whether the effect differs between adenocarcinoma and non-adenocarcinoma. I also registered a NFE2L2 KEAP1-loss comparison within TP53-loss cells to test whether the reversed KEAP1-loss effect remains present in a p53-null context. These are dataset-level association tests, not causal tests. Existing untested claims H24, H27, H31, H32, H34-H36, H22, and the MYC-amplification outcomes H2, H5, and H11 remain useful for closing out secondary and negative-control exploration after H15 validation is prioritized.",
 "research_notes": "Synthesis update after validation. Validated accepted main associations: H12 SMARCA4 loss -> stronger SMARCA2 dependency (R9 discovery, R13 validation); H16 MSI-high -> stronger WRN dependency (R12 discovery, R39 validation); H17 KEAP1 loss -> weaker NFE2L2 dependency (R6 discovery, R26 validation). Validated accepted context: H21 MSI-high WRN effect within adenocarcinoma (R17 discovery, R40 validation); close further context. Accepted but unvalidated main association: H15 TP53 wild-type -> stronger USP7 dependency. Internal support: overall R11 +0.802, CDKN2A-intact H28/R21 +0.800, CDKN2A-loss H41/R31 +0.808. Next validation priority: H15. Next registered robustness tests: USP7 TP53 WT within KEAP1-loss; USP7 interaction by lineage subtype; NFE2L2 KEAP1 loss within TP53-loss. Keep existing untested context/negative-control claims queued as secondary: H27, H24, H31, H32, H34-H36, H22, H2/H5/H11. Negative controls and interactions remain null: H37-H48 closed/rejected except H41 accepted context. EGFR H3 deferred; analyze H22 or another decisive context only if EGFR remains useful. All conclusions are associations in the supplied dataset, not causal or external generalizable claims."
