  "narrative": "All estimates are interpreted exactly as signed to the registered hypothesis direction. For the direction -1 MDM2 main contrasts, a positive estimate means the exposed group has a more negative MDM2 dependency score, i.e. stronger MDM2 dependency, than the comparator; for direction -1 interactions, a positive estimate means the CDKN2A-loss contrast is stronger in the named subgroup than in its complement; for the direction +1 USP7 contrast, a positive estimate would mean weaker USP7 dependency in CDKN2A-loss cells. H134 and H135 test the CDKN2A-loss effect separately in TP53 wild-type and TP53-loss cells. The signed estimates are +0.119 with interval +0.079 to +0.158 in TP53 wild-type cells and +0.111 with interval +0.035 to +0.186 in TP53-loss cells. Both are large relative to the recurring near-null dependency effects seen in this run and are above the practical 10% threshold on the MDM2 score scale, with intervals excluding null. I therefore accept H134 and H135 and close these specific subgroup tests. H136, the TP53-loss interaction, is -0.008 with interval -0.093 to +0.077; there is no evidence that TP53 loss modifies the CDKN2A effect, although the interval is not so narrow as to rule out a moderate interaction. I treat H136 as unsupported and close it because the stratified main effects are consistent. H137 tests MTAP loss overall on MDM2 dependency and H148 tests MTAP loss among TP53 wild-type cells. Their signed estimates are only +0.019 with interval -0.008 to +0.045 and +0.024 with interval -0.005 to +0.054, respectively. These positive trends are below the practical threshold I am applying on the MDM2 scale and their intervals include no effect; I therefore reject both as not scientifically meaningful evidence for MTAP loss alone. H149 tests TP53 wild-type versus loss among MTAP-intact cells and is essentially null, +0.003 with interval -0.025 to +0.031, supporting the conclusion that neither MTAP status nor TP53 status alone accounts for the accepted CDKN2A-MDM2 axis. H138 tests CDKN2A loss among MTAP-intact cells and is robust, +0.105 with interval +0.067 to +0.143; I accept and close it. H139 tests CDKN2A loss among MTAP-deleted cells and gives the largest point estimate, +0.165 with interval +0.081 to +0.249. The discovery interval is favorable, but the MTAP-deleted cells are a smaller and more co-deletion-enriched subset, and H140, the interaction for stronger effect in MTAP loss, is only +0.060 with interval -0.032 to +0.152 and does not establish reliable effect modification. Because this context is mechanistically important and potentially confounded by larger 9p21 deletions, I request independent validation of H139 and keep it unresolved pending that validation. H140 itself does not support an interaction conclusion; I reject and close it while noting that a moderate positive interaction remains possible but unproven. H141 tests CDKN2A-MDM2 in high-Cas9-quality screens and is robust, +0.116 with interval +0.070 to +0.161, so I accept and close this screen-quality check. H142 tests USP7 dependency in the opposite direction, expecting weaker USP7 dependency in CDKN2A-loss cells, and is null: -0.002 with interval -0.043 to +0.038. H146 tests SMARCA2 dependency associated with CDKN2A loss and is also null, +0.009 with interval -0.032 to +0.050. Both reject and close; together they support specificity of the CDKN2A-MDM2 association rather than a broad dependency-state artifact. Overall, these results strengthen the interpretation that the CDKN2A-MDM2 association is robust across TP53 status, MTAP-intact status, MTAP-deleted status pending validation, and screen-quality selection, and that MTAP and TP53 main effects do not explain it. They remain dataset-level associations, not causal or externally generalizable claims.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 10 appraise. CDKN2A-MDM2 axis remains central and robust. H132 already accepted after independent validation. New stratified evidence: H134 accept in TP53 wild-type (+0.119), H135 accept in TP53 loss (+0.111), H136 reject TP53 interaction null; H138 accept in MTAP-intact (+0.105), H139 unresolved pending validation in MTAP-loss (+0.165), H140 reject MTAP interaction unsupported; H137/H148 reject MTAP main effects small and null-compatible; H149 reject TP53 main effect null in MTAP-intact; H141 accept high-Cas9 robustness (+0.116); H142 and H146 reject USP7/SMARCA2 specificity checks null. Interpretation: CDKN2A loss association with stronger MDM2 dependency is not explained by MTAP loss or TP53 status alone and not a broad copy-number/p53 pathway artifact across tested unrelated dependencies. Validation request H139 is intended to resolve whether MTAP-deleted context truly amplifies the effect or whether this is small-sample/co-deletion noise. If H139 validates, treat CDKN2A-MDM2 as contextually stronger among MTAP-deleted cells while still noting 9p21 co-deletion confounding; if H139 fails, keep the main effect and the stable MTAP-intact/TP53 contexts and close the context-specific MTAP-loss interpretation. Remaining lower-priority CDKN2A checks are histology H145, high-aneuploidy H150, TP53 effect within CDKN2A-loss H144, and CDKN2A/TP53/MTAP triple wild-type eligibility H147. These are secondary unless H139 creates a need for additional context resolution. Existing accepted axes remain SMARCA4-SMARCA2, MSI-WRN, TP53 wildtype-USP7, KEAP1-NFE2L2, and PTEN-STAT3, with negative and nonreplicating interaction results supporting pathway specificity. All conclusions remain dataset-level associations and not causal or generalizable claims.",
