  "narrative": "All estimates are interpreted exactly as signed to the registered direction. For the direction -1 USP7, MDM2, SMARCA2, STAT3, and NFE2L2-related tests below, a positive main-effect estimate means the exposed group has a more negative dependency score, i.e. stronger dependency, than the comparator; for the direction +1 USP7 MTAP test, a positive estimate would mean weaker USP7 dependency in MTAP-deleted cells; for the direction +1 NFE2L2 KEAP1 test, a positive estimate means weaker NFE2L2 dependency with KEAP1 loss, as previously established. H64 accepts the robustness of the USP7 axis within MTAP-deleted cells: TP53 wild-type versus TP53 loss in MTAP-deleted cells has signed estimate +0.766, interval +0.719 to +0.813, a very large, precise association consistent with the validated overall USP7 TP53-wild-type effect. H147 accepts the CDKN2A-MDM2 association in a mechanistically cleaner context, TP53 wild-type and MTAP intact: +0.106, interval +0.063 to +0.150, just above the practical dependency-score scale and excluding null. H163 accepts CDKN2A-MDM2 robustness in high-Cas9 MTAP-deleted cells: +0.158, interval +0.056 to +0.261. H164 accepts CDKN2A-MDM2 robustness in low-aneuploidy TP53-wild-type cells: +0.103, interval +0.060 to +0.147. These are context confirmations of the main CDKN2A-MDM2 association, not independent proof of amplification by MTAP deletion. H165, H167, H168, and H169 accept broad robustness of accepted axes: USP7 TP53 wild-type effect in MTAP-intact cells +0.810; SMARCA4-loss SMARCA2 effect in MTAP-deleted cells +0.779; KEAP1-loss weaker NFE2L2 dependency in MTAP-deleted cells +0.807; and PTEN-loss stronger STAT3 dependency in TP53-wild-type cells +0.287. These large estimates are highly unlikely to be false positives driven by multiple subgroup testing. H161 does not support the claim that MTAP loss meaningfully adds MDM2 dependency among CDKN2A-loss TP53-wild-type cells: signed estimate +0.065, interval -0.034 to +0.164, below the practical threshold at the point estimate and including no effect. This is not proof of no MTAP effect, but the discovery evidence is insufficient and does not justify accepting a context amplification. H162 rejects any MTAP loss effect among CDKN2A-intact TP53-wild-type MDM2 dependency cells: +0.009, interval -0.015 to +0.033. H166 rejects a meaningful MTAP-only effect on USP7 among TP53-wild-type cells: +0.018, interval -0.004 to +0.041, a near-null specificity check. H170 rejects TP53 wild-type versus loss as a driver of MDM2 dependency within MTAP-deleted cells: +0.033, interval -0.026 to +0.093. Together, these conditional and specificity tests weaken the hypothesis that MTAP co-deletion or TP53 status amplifies or explains the CDKN2A-MDM2 association, while leaving the main CDKN2A-MDM2 association accepted. I therefore reassess H139: its direct independent validation remains attenuated and inconclusive, and the new conditional tests do not establish reliable MTAP-deletion-specific amplification; because validation capacity is exhausted and the exact context has already been explored, H139 is closed as unresolved rather than accepted. No independent validation is requested because no new validation requests remain.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 11 post-appraise. No validation capacity remains; all conclusions come from discovery evidence plus prior validations. Signed interpretation remains: direction -1 positive main effect = stronger dependency in exposed; direction +1 positive main effect = weaker dependency in exposed. MTAP/CDKN2A/MDM2 question: CDKN2A-loss MDM2-dependency association is accepted overall and robust in TP53-wild-type, MTAP-intact, high-Cas9, MTAP-deleted high-Cas9, and low-aneuploidy TP53-wild-type contexts. MTAP-specific amplification is not supported: H139 direct validation inconclusive, H161/H162/H140 do not establish added MTAP effect or interaction; H139 closed unresolved. MTAP and TP53 main effects on USP7, STAT3, and MDM2 are near-null in the tested contexts, supporting pathway specificity. Newly accepted robustness claims: H64 USP7 TP53-wild-type effect in MTAP-deleted; H147 CDKN2A-MDM2 in TP53-WT MTAP-intact; H163 CDKN2A-MDM2 in high-Cas9 MTAP-deleted; H164 CDKN2A-MDM2 in low-aneuploidy TP53-WT; H165 USP7 TP53-WT effect in MTAP-intact; H167 SMARCA4-SMARCA2 effect in MTAP-deleted; H168 KEAP1 weaker NFE2L2 dependency in MTAP-deleted; H169 PTEN-STAT3 effect in TP53-WT. Newly rejected: H161 MTAP among CDKN2A-loss TP53-WT; H162 MTAP among CDKN2A-intact TP53-WT; H166 MTAP effect on USP7 in TP53-WT; H170 TP53 status on MDM2 in MTAP-deleted. Main accepted dataset-level associations: SMARCA4 loss/SMARCA2 dependency; MSI-high/WRN dependency; TP53 wild-type/USP7 dependency; KEAP1 loss/weaker NFE2L2 dependency; PTEN loss/STAT3 dependency; CDKN2A loss/MDM2 dependency. These remain dataset-level associations, not causal or generalizable claims. Future allocation should prioritize genuinely new predictor-outcome axes or orthogonal robustness checks of accepted large effects, not further MTAP-CDKN2A interaction microtesting. Use practical threshold around 0.10 for moderate dependency-scale effects and require interval excluding null plus consistency; near-null 0.