  "narrative": "All estimates are interpreted exactly as signed to the registered hypothesis direction. For direction -1 hypotheses, a positive estimate supports stronger dependency in the exposed group, because the raw contrast is negative, i.e. more negative for exposed than comparator. For H176, direction +1 and positive estimate supports weaker NFE2L2 dependency with KEAP1 loss, consistent with the earlier accepted reversal. The low-Cas9 robustness panel H171-H176 supports robustness of the main accepted axes under cas9_activity_pct <=67.7. H171 SMARCA4-loss associated with stronger SMARCA2 dependency in low-Cas9 screens: +0.754, CI +0.712 to +0.797, n=[85,345]. H172 MSI-high associated with stronger WRN dependency: +0.798, CI +0.732 to +0.864, n=[27,403]. H173 TP53 wild-type status associated with stronger USP7 dependency: +0.795, CI +0.751 to +0.838, n=[340,90]. H175 PTEN-loss associated with stronger STAT3 dependency: +0.372, CI +0.268 to +0.476, n=[73,357]. H176 KEAP1 loss associated with weaker NFE2L2 dependency: +0.799, CI +0.751 to +0.847, n=[84,346]. These effects are large or very large relative to the dependency-score scale, intervals exclude zero, and they are broadly consistent with the previously accepted main axes. I therefore accept H171, H172, H173, H175, and H176 and close them as completed low-Cas9 robustness checks. This reduces concern that the accepted SMARCA2, WRN, USP7, STAT3, and NFE2L2 associations depend on high-Cas9 screens. H174 tests CDKN2A loss and MDM2 dependency in low-Cas9 screens: +0.109, CI +0.046 to +0.172, n=[89,341]. This is not attenuated relative to the main CDKN2A-MDM2 axis and excludes null, but it is near the practical 0.10 threshold and imprecise. I accept it as context-supporting, while noting that the magnitude is less certain than the large axes. The accepted main CDKN2A-MDM2 association remains the primary claim. Context checks for accepted axes are also supportive. H150 tests CDKN2A loss and MDM2 dependency in high-aneuploidy cells: +0.138, CI +0.064 to +0.212, n=[105,396]. H180 tests the same association in screen_batch batch_a: +0.119, CI +0.052 to +0.187, n=[93,426]. H181 tests SMARCA4 loss and SMARCA2 dependency in high-aneuploidy cells: +0.759, CI +0.721 to +0.798, n=[102,399]. H182 tests TP53 wild-type and USP7 dependency in high-aneuploidy cells: +0.791, CI +0.751 to +0.831, n=[391,110]. These intervals exclude null and magnitudes remain compatible with the accepted main axes, so I accept H150, H180, H181, and H182 and close them. They argue against the hypothesis that the MDM2, SMARCA2, or USP7 associations are primarily driven by high aneuploidy or batch_a composition, although they do not establish causality or external generalizability. The two negative tests are clear. H178 asks whether MSI-high cells have stronger STAT3 dependency overall: +0.016, CI -0.027 to +0.059. The point estimate is near null and the interval includes no effect, so I reject the claim of a meaningful MSI-high STAT3 association in this dataset. H179 tests BRAF-mutant versus BRAF-wild-type dependency within KRAS-wild-type cells: -0.019, CI -0.051 to +0.013. The signed estimate is slightly opposite to the registered direction, tiny, and includes null. I reject the claim of a meaningful BRAF-mutation effect on BRAF dependency in the KRAS-wild-type context. No independent validation is requested because no new validation requests remain. Overall, these results strengthen the evidence that the major accepted axes are dataset-level technical and genomic context robust: SMARCA4 loss/SMARCA2, MSI-high/WRN, TP53 wild-type/USP7, KEAP1 loss/weaker NFE2L2, PTEN loss/STAT3, and CDKN2A loss/MDM2, with the CDKN2A-MDM2 magnitude closer to the practical threshold and more uncertain than the very large axes.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 12 appraise. All estimates are signed; do not multiply by direction again. Low-Cas9 robustness is now complete for the six major axes: H171 SMARCA4 loss/SMARCA2, H172 MSI-high/WRN, H173 TP53 wild-type/USP7, H174 CDKN2A loss/MDM2, H175 PTEN loss/STAT3, and H176 KEAP1 loss/weaker NFE2L2. Acceptance: very large axes remain ~0.75-0.80 in low-Cas9 screens; STAT3 PTEN ~0.37; MDM2 CDKN2A ~0.11 but lower CI ~0.046, accepted as context support near threshold, not definitive magnitude proof. Context robustness accepted: H150 high-aneuploidy MDM2 CDKN2A +0.138, H180 batch_a MDM2 CDKN2A +0.119, H181 high-aneuploidy SMARCA2 +0.759, H182 high-aneuploidy USP7 +0.791. Negative: H178 MSI-high STAT3 +0.016 CI includes null; H179 BRAF-mutant BRAF dependency in KRAS-WT -0.019 CI includes null. No validation capacity remains; do not request validation. Keep accepted main axes closed. Future exploration, if any, should prioritize remaining untested predictor-outcome pairs or interactions only if they can be clearly linked to current accepted axes and are likely to add information, because many main axes are closed and MTAP-specific amplification remains unresolved/negative. Avoid re-testing accepted main effects unless asking a new mechanistic/technical question. Maintain practical benchmark: absolute dependency-score differences near or above 0.10 with CI excluding zero may be accepted when supported by larger prior effects; very large ~0.8 are decisive; near-null 0.01-0.03 with CI crossing zero are rejected. These remain dataset-level associations in supplied lung-cancer-like models, not causal or generalizable claims."
