  "narrative": "Synthesis: All estimates are interpreted exactly as signed to the registered hypothesis direction; for direction -1, positive means the exposed group has a more negative, i.e. stronger, dependency score than the comparator. The H139 response deadline concerns whether CDKN2A loss has a meaningfully stronger association with MDM2 dependency specifically in MTAP-loss-positive lines. The discovery estimate was +0.165 (95% CI +0.081 to +0.249), but the independent validation estimate was +0.079 with the stricter independent interval -0.039 to +0.196. The validation point estimate is below the 0.10 dependency-score-unit practical threshold and its interval includes no effect, so it does not confirm a meaningful MTAP-specific amplification. I therefore reject H139 as an established dataset-level association. This is not a proof of zero, but the independent evidence does not support MTAP co-deletion as a reliable modifier beyond the main CDKN2A-MDM2 effect.\n\nFinal supported findings: The supplied dataset supports several dataset-level association axes. SMARCA4 loss is associated with much stronger SMARCA2 dependency, with main effect about +0.78 and validated about +0.80; it is robust in adenocarcinoma, low-Cas9 screens, high-aneuploidy cells, MTAP-loss-positive eligibility, and other accepted context checks. MSI-high is associated with much stronger WRN dependency, main about +0.79 and validated about +0.81; it is robust across lineage subtype, BRCA2-loss-negative, adherent culture, low-Cas9 screens, batch_a, and adequate-Cas9 eligibility. TP53 wild-type status is associated with much stronger USP7 dependency, about +0.80 after validation; it is robust in CDKN2A-loss and CDKN2A-intact subgroups, adherent culture, batch_a, low-Cas9 screens, MTAP-loss-negative eligibility, and high-aneuploidy cells. KEAP1 loss is associated with much weaker NFE2L2 dependency, represented by the accepted reversal H17 with validated estimate about +0.80, and robust in low-Cas9, batch_a, STK11-loss-positive, MTAP-loss-positive, and adequacy-eligibility contexts. PTEN loss is associated with stronger STAT3 dependency, main about +0.27 and validated about +0.31; it is robust across batch, Cas9 eligibility, culture, lineage, low/intermediate IFN-gamma signature, SLFN11-high, PIK3CA-positive, TP53 wild-type, and low-Cas9 contexts. CDKN2A loss is associated with stronger MDM2 dependency, main about +0.117 and validated +0.100 with independent interval excluding null; it is robust in TP53 wild-type and TP53-loss subgroups, MTAP-loss-negative eligibility, high-Cas9 and low-Cas9 screens, batch_a, high-aneuploidy, low-aneuploidy with TP53 wild-type, and several other accepted context checks.\n\nNegative or unsupported findings: Many nominally plausible gene-state to dependency associations are near-null or unsupported. BRAF V600E is not meaningfully associated with BRAF dependency, including in KRAS-wild-type eligibility. KRAS mutation is not robustly associated with KRAS dependency; the validation estimate is essentially null. EGFR amplification is not associated with EGFR dependency in overall, adenocarcinoma, KRAS-wild-type, or STK11-wild-type contexts, and EGFR amplification in KRAS-wild-type cells did not support stronger STAT3 dependency after validation. ERBB2 amplification is not associated with ERBB2 or TMED10 dependency, and not associated with STAT3 dependency. MYC amplification is not associated with DHX9, KIF18A, or RPL11 dependency overall or in MYC-expression-high eligibility. Research markers D, E, and F show no meaningful associations with the tested dependencies. Many interaction hypotheses fail to show modification: SMARCA4-loss SMARCA2 effects are not modified by ARID1A loss, lineage subtype, TP53 loss, KEAP1 loss, or STK11 loss; TP53 wild-type USP7 effects are not modified by CDKN2A loss, KEAP1 loss, MTAP-loss-positive status, aneuploidy, or lineage in accepted interaction tests; PTEN-loss STAT3 effects are not supported as modified by PIK3CA mutation, SLFN11 expression, lineage subtype, TP53 loss, STK11 loss, high IFN-gamma, or ifn-gamma above zero; CDKN2A-loss MDM2 effects are not meaningfully modified by TP53 loss or MTAP loss as an interaction; and MSI-high WRN effects are not meaningfully modified by lineage subtype or high mutation burden in tested interaction analyses. The MTAP-specific amplification of CDKN2A-MDM2 is not confirmed and is now rejected as an established association.\n\nUnresolved uncertainty: Deferred or unresolved subgroup/context claims do not materially alter the main supported set. Biological mechanisms, causal direction, therapeutic relevance, and external generalizability remain unestablished. The MTAP co-deletion question is at most uncertain and likely unsupported as a modifier: discovery suggested amplification but independent validation was attenuated and imprecise, and the interaction test did not establish modification. Technical robustness within this dataset is much stronger than it was earlier because the major axes persist under low Cas9 activity, different batches, aneuploidy strata, culture type, and lineage subsets, but this only reduces some dataset-specific confounding concerns; it does not prove causality.\n\nMost informative next analysis: No independent validation requests remain. If further external work is possible, the highest-value step is independent replication of the accepted axes in an external cohort, especially the intermediate CDKN2A-MDM2 and PTEN-STAT3 effects, and a larger pre-specified test of whether MTAP co-deletion modifies CDKN2A-MDM2. Within the supplied dataset, the next most useful analysis would be a summary of conditional dependence of accepted axes on screen-quality and genomic-instability covariates using the existing Welch comparisons, but current evidence already supports robustness and additional low-power subgroup tests are unlikely to add much.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 12 synthesis complete. Interpreting all returned estimates exactly as signed; do not multiply by direction again. H139 due response assessed with R126 and R133 and rejected as established: discovery cdkn2a_loss vs WT within mtap_loss_positive was +0.165 CI +0.081 to +0.249, but independent validation was +0.079 independent CI -0.039 to +0.196, below the 0.10 practical threshold and not excluding null. This rejects MTAP-specific amplification of the CDKN2A-MDM2 axis as a reliable dataset-level association, not a proof of zero. Main CDKN2A-MDM2 axis remains accepted from H132: discovery +0.117, independent validation +0.100 CI +0.049 to +0.151; robustness accepted in multiple contexts including H134, H135, H138, H141, H143/H144 context, H147, H150, H163, H164, H174, H180.\n\nAccepted major axes and magnitudes: SMARCA4 loss -> much stronger SMARCA2 dependency ~0.78 to 0.80, validated, robust low Cas9, high aneuploidy, adenocarcinoma, MTAP-loss eligibility. MSI-high -> much stronger WRN dependency ~0.79 to 0.81, validated, robust across lineage, BRCA2-WT, adherent, low Cas9, batch_a, adequate Cas9. TP53 wild-type -> much stronger USP7 dependency ~0.80, validated, robust in CDKN2A loss/WT, adherent, batch_a, low Cas9, MTAP-WT eligibility, high aneuploidy. KEAP1 loss -> much weaker NFE2L2 dependency, accepted reversal H17 ~0.80 validated, robust in low Cas9, batch_a, STK11-loss-positive, MTAP-loss-positive, adequate Cas9. PTEN loss -> stronger STAT3 dependency ~0.27 main, validated ~0.31, robust in batch, Cas9, culture, lineage, low IFN, SLFN-high, PIK3CA-positive, TP53-WT, low Cas9. CDKN2A loss -> stronger MDM2 dependency ~0.10 to 0.12 validated, robust but near threshold; accepted as meaningful within dataset but less decisive magnitude than very large axes.\n\nNegative/unsupported: BRAF mutation vs BRAF dependency near null, including KRAS-WT; KRAS mutation vs KRAS dependency not supported and validated near null; EGFR amp vs EGFR and STAT3 not supported; ERBB2 amp vs ERBB2/TMED10/STAT3 near null; MYC amp vs DHX9/KIF18A/RPL11 near null; marker D/E/F tests near null; many interaction hypotheses not supported, including lineage, PIK3CA, TP53, KEAP1, ARID1A, STK11, IFN-gamma, SLFN11, aneuploidy, mutation-burden, and MTAP interaction for CDKN2A-MDM2. H92 rejected due validation; H103 rejected; H114/H120 rejected after validation; H139 now rejected due validation.\n\nValidation capacity exhausted; do not request validation. Future useful work outside current run: external replication of accepted axes, especially CDKN2A-MDM2 and PTEN-STAT3, and larger MTAP interaction test if MTAP-specific amplification is scientifically important. Within supplied dataset, main axes closed and robustness complete; additional low-power subgroups less informative."
}

