  "narrative": "All estimates are interpreted exactly as signed to the registered hypothesis direction; no additional sign multiplication was applied. The high-ploidy eligibility panel H208-H213 shows that all six previously accepted predictor-dependency axes remain strongly associated in this genomic-context subset. H208 SMARCA4 loss versus SMARCA2 dependency is +0.769, 95% CI +0.730 to +0.807. H209 MSI-high versus WRN dependency is +0.790, CI +0.729 to +0.850. H210 TP53 wild-type versus TP53 loss versus USP7 dependency is +0.797, CI +0.758 to +0.836. H211 KEAP1 loss versus weaker NFE2L2 dependency is +0.808, CI +0.766 to +0.849. H212 PTEN loss versus STAT3 dependency is +0.228, CI +0.127 to +0.329. H213 CDKN2A loss versus MDM2 dependency is +0.106, CI +0.036 to +0.175. All intervals exclude the null in the hypothesized direction. The first four are very large on the dependency-score scale; the last two are intermediate but comparable to their already accepted and validated main effects, and are practically meaningful relative to the typical dependency-score scale. I accept these as dataset-specific context robustness results, not causal or externally generalizable claims. Some exposed cell counts are modest, especially MSI-high in high ploidy, so exact uncertainty is wider there, but the intervals remain decisive.\n\nH226 resolves the broader upper-half screen-quality context for CDKN2A loss and MDM2 dependency: signed effect +0.132, CI +0.081 to +0.184. This supports the accepted CDKN2A-MDM2 association in a broader high-ROC-AUC population and reduces concern from the underpowered very-high-quality subset H207. It should not be read as confirmation of exact very-high ROC-AUC subgroup specificity; H207 remains a narrow unresolved subset.\n\nH227 and H228 provide direct EMT-stratum contrasts for PTEN loss and STAT3 dependency. The PTEN-loss association is positive and CI-excluding in high EMT (+0.378, CI +0.261 to +0.495) and in low EMT (+0.237, CI +0.179 to +0.295