  "narrative": "No new validation results and no response deadlines were delivered. assessments_due is empty and voluntary validation capacity is exhausted, so I make no claim status changes. All estimates below are interpreted exactly as already signed to the registered hypothesis direction; no additional sign multiplication is applied. For direction -1 claims, a positive signed estimate means the raw exposed-minus-comparator contrast is negative, i.e. the exposed group has a raw more negative dependency score and therefore stronger dependency. For the KEAP1-loss NFE2L2 claims with direction +1, a positive signed estimate means KEAP1-loss lines have raw weaker, less negative NFE2L2 dependency. All conclusions are associations among measured variables in this supplied lung-lineage CRISPR screen dataset, not causal, synthetic-lethal, therapeutic, or externally generalizable claims. Supported findings: the evidence base now strongly supports six dataset-specific genotype-context axes. First, SMARCA4 loss is associated with much stronger SMARCA2 dependency, H12/R9 +0.784 95% CI +0.765 to +0.803, independently replicated by R13 +0.800 CI +0.768 to +0.832. This pattern is robust in adenocarcinoma context H25/R19 +0.777 CI +0.755 to +0.799, in ARID1A-intact lines H60/R49 +0.777 CI +0.756 to +0.798, across screen-quality and proliferation contexts, and in KRAS-mutant lines H233/R208 +0.774 CI +0.733 to +0.814. Second, MSI-high is associated with much stronger WRN dependency, H16/R12 +0.790 CI +0.760 to +0.819, replicated by R39 +0.807 CI +0.759 to +0.855, with adenocarcinoma context H21/R17 +0.784 CI +0.748 to +0.820 and validation R40 +0.813 CI +0.754 to +0.872. Third, TP53 wild type, coded as TP53_loss exposure 0 versus comparator 1, is associated with much stronger USP7 dependency than TP53 loss, H15/R11 +0.802 CI +0.782 to +0.822, replicated by R53 +0.799 CI +0.769 to +0.828, and robust across many contexts including KRAS-mutant lines H232/R207 +0.783 CI +0.741 to +0.826. Fourth, KEAP1 loss is associated with much weaker NFE2L2 dependency, H17/R6 +0.796 CI +0.776 to +0.816, replicated by R26 +0.801 CI +0.772 to +0.829, with KRAS-mutant context H234/R209 +0.805 CI +0.767 to +0.843. Fifth, PTEN loss is associated with stronger STAT3 dependency, H81/R63 +0.267 CI +0.215 to +0.319, replicated by R66 +0.310 CI +0.231 to +0.388, and observed in many strata including KRAS-mutant lines H230/R203 +0.249 CI +0.139 to +0.358, high-EMT stratum H227/R201 +0.378 CI +0.261 to +0.495, and low-EMT stratum H228/R202 +0.237 CI +0.179 to +0.295. Sixth, CDKN2A loss is associated with stronger MDM2 dependency, H132/R119 +0.117 CI +0.082 to +0.152, replicated by R120 +0.100 CI +0.049 to +0.151, with KRAS-mutant context H231/R204 +0.168 CI +0.092 to +0.243, broad upper-half screen-quality context H226/R200 +0.132 CI +0.081 to +0.184, and lower-half screen-quality context H229/R206 +0.103 CI +0.056 to +0.150. The four very large axes have interval widths and point magnitudes far beyond null on the dependency-score scale; the PTEN-STAT3 and CDKN2A-MDM2 effects are intermediate but CI-excluding, replicated, and meet the task relevance threshold as dataset-specific associations. Context robustness: the same axes persist across many biologically and technical subsets, including high ploidy H208-H213, KRAS mutation H232-H234, screen-quality strata H226/H229/H202-H207, EMT strata H227/H228, and lineage subtype or culture contexts where tested. Negative findings: many intuitive matched-gene dependencies are absent or too small. BRAF V600E does not support stronger BRAF dependency H1/R1. KRAS mutation does not support stronger KRAS dependency H6/R4, with near-null validation R80. EGFR amplification does not support stronger EGFR dependency H3/R2 or in adenocarcinoma, KRAS-WT, or combined contexts H18/R14, H33/R24, H128/R118. ERBB2 amplification does not support stronger ERBB2 or TMED10 dependency H4/R3, H14/R25, H127/R117. MYC amplification does not support stronger DHX9, KIF18A, RPL11, or MDM2 dependency H2/R108, H5/R109, H11/R110, H214/R188. RB1 loss does not support stronger MDM2 dependency H191/R172. NF1 loss does not support stronger BRAF dependency H189/R170. PTEN loss does not support stronger WRN or RPL11 dependency H219/R191 and H190/R171. KEAP1 loss does not support stronger WRN dependency H218/R190. MSI-high does not support stronger KIF18A dependency H193/R174. ARID1A loss does not support stronger WRN dependency H235/R205. Constructed research markers D/E/F show no meaningful associations H45/R35, H46/R36, H47/R37, H48/R38. Several effect-modifier hypotheses are negative or failed independent validation, including IFN-gamma modification of PTEN-STAT3 H92/R75 plus validation R79 and H103/R82 plus validation R93, and MTAP modification of CDKN2A-MDM2 H139/R126 plus validation R133. Unresolved or low-confidence questions: H207/R187 leaves a very-high screen-quality CDKN2A-MDM2 subset unresolved at +0.071 CI -0.006 to +0.149, but the broader upper-half quality result H226/R200 and lower-half result H229/R206 make this a low-priority precision question rather than a challenge to the main CDKN2A-MDM2 axis. H195/R176 suggests a possible EMT interaction for PTEN-STAT3 at +0.141 CI +0.011 to +0.271, but I treat the direct strata H227/H228 as the safer interpretation because the interaction lacks independent confirmation. H114/R100 is formally accepted at +0.044 CI +0.001 to +0.086 for EGFR amplification in KRAS-WT STAT3 dependency, but its validation R106 is not conclusive, so I regard it as a low-confidence secondary signal rather than a major axis. The direct continuous-threshold main-effect claims H236-H243, and likely H244-H246, returned invalid insufficient-cell-count diagnostics because the controller appears to evaluate exact-value exposure/comparator cells rather than threshold-defined groups; these are analysis-coding failures, not biological null evidence against MYC expression, growth rate, IFN-gamma, AXL, hypoxia, aneuploidy, or SLFN11 direct effects. The most informative next discovery analysis is H248, PTEN loss versus STAT3 dependency within high-AXL eligibility. This tests an accepted intermediate axis in a high-AXL resistance-like context, uses the valid eligibility/binary-exposure design, and directly addresses the earlier invalid direct AXL-threshold concern. If H248 persists, it further broadens PTEN-STAT3 robustness; if attenuated, it identifies a new context limitation. If budget remains, the next best active analyses are H247 for CDKN2A-MDM2 under faster growth and the lower-ploidy panel H249-H254 to complement the accepted high-ploidy robustness panel. No further independent validation can be requested because validation capacity is exhausted."
