  "narrative": "No assessments were due and voluntary validation capacity is exhausted, so no new validation was requested. I assessed all validation evidence present in the ledger against the registered hypothesis direction, interpreting returned estimates exactly as already signed and not applying any additional sign transformation. The central conclusion is that the supplied lung-lineage CRISPR screen dataset contains several large, reproducible, dataset-specific genotype dependency associations, while many direct matched-gene dependency hypotheses and effect-modifier hypotheses are absent or too uncertain to support. Six main axes are well supported. First, SMARCA4 loss is associated with much stronger SMARCA2 dependency, H12/R9 plus validation R13, with broad context robustness including adenocarcinoma H25/R19, ARID1A-intact lines H60/R49, fast and slow screen-quality contexts, high and low ploidy, KRAS-mutant lines H233/R208, MTAP-loss lines H167/R142, and lower-ploidy lines H249/R220. Second, MSI-high is associated with much stronger WRN dependency, H16/R12 plus validation R39, replicated in adenocarcinoma H21/R17 plus validation R40, and robust across many screen and genomic contexts including H55, H56, H57, H76, H152, H153, H172, H184, H203, H209, H254. Third, TP53 wild-type status, coded as exposure 0 versus comparator 1 for TP53 loss, is associated with much stronger USP7 dependency than TP53 loss, H15/R11 plus validation R53, with robustness across many contexts including KRAS-mutant lines H232/R207, adenocarcinoma H27/R166, and lower ploidy H251/R222. Fourth, KEAP1 loss is associated with much weaker NFE2L2 dependency, H17/R6 plus validation R26, robust in adenocarcinoma H20/R16, TP53-intact lines H31/R169, KRAS-mutant lines H234/R209, and lower-ploidy lines H250/R221. Fifth, PTEN loss is associated with stronger STAT3 dependency, H81/R63 plus validation R66, and robust across many contexts including lower ploidy H252/R223, high EMT H227/R201, low EMT H228/R202, high AXL eligibility H248/R219, TP53-intact H169/R144, PIK3CA-mutant subgroup H106/R85 plus validation R107, and KRAS-mutant lines H230/R203. Sixth, CDKN2A loss is associated with stronger MDM2 dependency, H132/R119 plus validation R120, robust across many contexts including fast-growth eligibility H247/R218, KRAS-mutant lines H231/R204, and broad screen-quality halves H226/R200 and H229/R206. These are dataset-specific associations, not causal, synthetic-lethal, therapeutic, or externally generalizable claims. Negative findings are also substantial. Matched-gene driver dependencies are largely absent: BRAF V600E does not support stronger BRAF dependency, H1/R1 and H179/R154; KRAS mutation does not support stronger KRAS dependency, H6/R4 with near-null validation R80; EGFR amplification does not support stronger EGFR dependency in main or constrained contexts, H3/R2, H18/R14, H33/R24, H128/R118; ERBB2 amplification does not support stronger ERBB2 or TMED10 dependency, H4/R3, H14/R25, H127/R117; MYC amplification does not support stronger DHX9, KIF18A, RPL11, or MDM2 dependency, H2/R108, H5/R109, H11/R110, H214/R188; PIK3CA mutation does not support weaker EGFR, ERBB2, or KRAS dependency among KRAS-wild-type lines or stronger MDM2 dependency among TP53-wild-type lines, H255-H258. Many broader tests are also negative, including RB1 loss against MDM2 H191/R172, NF1 loss against BRAF H189/R170, PTEN loss against WRN and RPL11 H219/R191 and H190/R171, KEAP1 loss against WRN H218/R190, MSI-high against KIF18A H193/R174, ARID1A loss against WRN H235/R205, and the constructed research markers D, E, and F H45-H48. Several effect-modifier or subgroup hypotheses have mixed discovery and validation evidence and should not be treated as accepted or firmly rejected. H92/R75 and validation R79, H103/R82 and validation R93, H120/R100 and validation R106, and H139/R126 and validation R133 all show discovery support for a direction but validation intervals that include the null, and in some cases opposite-point validation estimates. I therefore reclassified these four claims as unresolved rather than accepted or rejected. They represent possible secondary modifiers, subgroup effects, or chance discovery signals that remain unsupported at present. H195/R176 remains an unresolved EMT-interaction signal; I closed its investigation because the direct PTEN-loss STAT3 strata H227 and H228 are already robust and validation capacity is exhausted. The unresolved H207 very-high screen-quality CDKN2A-MDM2 subset R187 is a precision issue about attenuation under stricter quality filtering, not a challenge to the main axis. The invalid continuous-threshold main-effect claims H236-H243 and likely H244-H246 should be read as analysis-coding failures from exact-cell threshold handling, not as biological evidence against continuous predictors. The most informative next discovery work is to execute the remaining valid active claims H259-H266 rather than request more validation. H266 RB1 loss against STAT3 is the most novel direct predictor test. H259-H263 test persistence of accepted axes in faster-growing lines and can identify proliferation context as an important limitation. H264-H265 test receptor co-dependency logic among EGFR and ERBB2 amplification. No causal mechanism or therapeutic interpretation should be drawn from the current set.",
  "research_notes": "Final synthesis at iteration 18: six supported dataset-specific axes are SMARCA4-loss to stronger SMARCA2, MSI-high to stronger WRN, TP53-wild-type to stronger USP7, KEAP1-loss to weaker NFE2L2, PTEN-loss to stronger STAT3, and CDKN2A-loss to stronger MDM2. All have discovery CIs excluding null, several with independent validation, and broad context robustness across ploidy, screen quality, lineage subtype where tested, KRAS mutation, EMT strata, culture, growth quality, and high/low AXL. Mixed evidence reassessed: H92, H103, H120, and H139 are now unresolved closed because validation intervals include the null and sometimes point opposite; H195 remains unresolved closed due low priority and no validation capacity. Negative or low-confidence claims include direct matched-gene dependencies and PIK3CA direct bypass/MDM2 tests. Continuous exact-threshold claims are technical failures, not biological nulls. Voluntary validation capacity exhausted. Next priority: active valid H266 RB1-STAT3, H259-H263 fast-growth robustness, H264-H265 receptor cross-dependency. Do not propose repeated invalid continuous main effects or signature interactions."
