s interaction, is null and very wide, so there is no evidence that RB1 loss modifies the PTEN-loss STAT3 association. I therefore reject the interaction claim but leave H271, H273, and the parent H266 unresolved as possible modest dataset-specific RB1 associations. I close the line because voluntary validation capacity is exhausted and further effort is better directed to accepted-axis robustness. The serum-rich culture context strongly supports the main accepted axes: CDKN2A-loss MDM2 +0.114, interval +0.070 to +0.157; TP53-wild-type USP7 +0.800, interval +0.774 to +0.826; PTEN-loss STAT3 +0.286, interval +0.216 to +0.357. I accept and close H275, H276, and H277. The high-hypoxia KEAP1-loss NFE2L2 direct main effect is also robust, +0.754, interval +0.711 to +0.797, so H278 is accepted and closed. No validation is requested because the remaining new voluntary validation capacity is zero. All conclusions remain dataset-specific associations, not causality, synthetic lethality, therapeutic vulnerability, or external generalization.",
